# Host-level redirects. Read by Netlify and by Cloudflare Pages as-is; on
# nginx or Caddy the same three rules have to be written in that server's own
# syntax - see the note at the bottom.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the docs
#
# Documentation, the API reference and the SDK guide moved to their own site
# (docs/ in this repository, deployed to docs.rovie.africa). These three paths
# were linked from the header and the footer for months, so they have inbound
# links and whatever ranking those earned.
#
# 301, not 302: a permanent redirect is what passes that ranking to the new
# URL. A 302 tells a crawler to keep indexing the old one, which here is a page
# that no longer exists.
#
# routes/router.tsx also redirects these client-side. That is a fallback for
# hosts that ignore this file - it is a 200 with a JavaScript hop in it, which
# is not what a crawler needs. These rules are the real mechanism.

# Deep links first: /docs/quickstart has a real counterpart at the same slug,
# and sending it to the front page instead would throw away the specificity
# somebody's bookmark or blog post already had. The splat must precede the bare
# /docs rule - these are matched in order.
/docs/*             https://docs.rovie.africa/:splat   301!
/docs               https://docs.rovie.africa/start/quickstart/   301!

# These two had no sub-pages, so there is nothing to preserve. Each lands on
# its section's own front page rather than the docs homepage.
/api-reference      https://docs.rovie.africa/api/   301!
/sdk                https://docs.rovie.africa/sdks/overview/   301!

# ----------------------------------------------------------- Rovie Route
#
# Route is a separate product site. Its sign-in, sign-up and account pages
# must never remain under the umbrella origin: session cookies and the
# dashboard belong to route.rovie.africa.
/route              https://route.rovie.africa/                301!
/signin             https://route.rovie.africa/signin          301!
/signup             https://route.rovie.africa/signup          301!
/reset-password     https://route.rovie.africa/reset-password  301!
/dashboard/*        https://route.rovie.africa/dashboard/:splat 301!
/dashboard          https://route.rovie.africa/dashboard       301!
/login              https://route.rovie.africa/signin          301!
/register           https://route.rovie.africa/signup          301!

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- SPA
#
# Everything else is served by the app. This has to come LAST: it matches every
# path, so any rule below it is dead.
#
# 200, not 301 - the URL stays what the visitor asked for and React Router
# reads it. The prerendered per-route files written by vite/seo-plugin.js are
# real files, so the host serves those before falling through to here, which is
# what puts the right <title> in front of a crawler.
/*                  /index.html   200

